/* posix.spec -- what build/posixgen.c measures: every POSIX constant and struct layout that
   tiko-rt's and pkg/std's '__FB_UNIX__' code (and the compiler's own host code) names.

   C, read by the C preprocessor: build/posixgen.c includes it twice, see the macros there.
   A name that exists on one OS only goes under '#ifdef' of the name itself (or __linux__ /
   __APPLE__ for a struct member), so one spec serves every POSIX host. A tiko source that
   names a constant or field this file does not list fails to compile -- add it here and
   rerun build/posixgen.sh on each POSIX host, never type a value into a .tiko.

   Struct types are named struct_<C tag> (struct_stat), so they can never collide with the C
   function of the same name -- stat(), sigaction(), flock(), statvfs() -- in tiko's
   case-insensitive namespace. C typedef names (sigset_t, pthread_mutex_t) are kept. A field
   whose C name is a tiko keyword gets a trailing '_' (inotify_event's len_). */

